      "title": "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parabola"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "27089061-5d92-5d5f-9ba8-56a353596e21",
      ":question/problem": "![](/tmp/course-academy-g2-readonly-tly0pcma/17592186166867/caller-hard/generated/1b5ecb611fcbee7a90c56f1b4e307c0e302ac672c26cd39d8512177ca22955d3.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "fa7f3566-b355-5307-8d46-21e6263bbde0",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "309670c4-3085-5d86-8582-cc413a0ac295",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{6y}{49}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "9705f42f-d919-5958-9ca6-53a4a18ba5b1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{49}{6y}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "829c66b6-ee86-5017-b1d6-2979239bea14",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{49}{3y}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "e09c150b-7985-5617-9c95-9ea822a889e0",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{49}{6y}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "9955e4e4-da05-5460-8995-f43ec89ea1e9",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{49}{6}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "e09c150b-7985-5617-9c95-9ea822a889e0"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-3,-7).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-3$ and $y=-7$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-7)^{2} & =4p(-3) \\\\ 49 & =-12p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{49}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-\\frac{49}{3}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{49}{3}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{49}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{49}{6y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard"
    },
