    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0bf2d369-c7fe-5d92-a242-dddf2138bd1b",
      ":question/problem": "![](/tmp/course-academy-g2-readonly-tly0pcma/17592186166867/caller-hard/generated/a7e030e51f92bba80dec3eeeb1f49b0343171a371ce3618f8f110b1483ad0724.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "542d3478-27bd-501a-a9f0-6c99aa5b1668",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "f6bb7a17-18bd-5740-ba2e-a3b7a8e554bf",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{32}{3y}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "f6bb7a17-18bd-5740-ba2e-a3b7a8e554bf"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-3,-8).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-3$ and $y=-8$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)^{2} & =4p(-3) \\\\ 64 & =-12p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-\\frac{64}{3}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{64}{3}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{64}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{32}{3y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard"
    },
